.TH GFT 1 "2026" "gft" "GitHub Fetch Tool"
.SH NAME
gft \- GitHub Fetch Tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gft
.RI [ options ]
.RB [ \-\- ]
.I user/repo
.RI [ tag ]
.br
.B gft
.BR update " | " delete " | " stash
.RI [ action ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gft
is a lightweight command-line tool to fetch release information, list binary
assets, and download from any GitHub project \[em] without authentication.
.PP
It scrapes GitHub release pages directly, requiring no token setup and avoiding
API rate limit issues. When the
.B gh
CLI is installed and authenticated, gft reads release data from the GitHub API
through it; the JSON output keeps the same keys either way (see
.BR "JSON OUTPUT" ).
.SH USAGE
.TP
.BI "gft " user/repo
Show latest release info
.TP
.BI "gft " "user/repo tag"
Show info for a specific release tag
.TP
.BI "gft " "user/repo v1.0..v2.0"
Compare two releases
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options: every following argument is a repository or a tag, never an
option or a command (e.g.
.BR "gft \-\- update/x" ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show gft version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-update
Check if a newer version of gft is available. Versions are compared
numerically, ignoring a leading \fBv\fR: an older gft reports an update, an
equal one is up to date, and a newer one (a development build) is reported as
newer than the latest release. When gft is installed as a package (see
.BR "PACKAGE INSTALLATION" ),
the update message shows the apt command instead of
.BR "gft \-\-upgrade" .
.TP
.B \-\-upgrade
Upgrade gft to the latest version in-place. Does nothing and exits with status
1 when gft is installed as a package (see
.BR "PACKAGE INSTALLATION" ).
Never installs an older version.
.TP
.B \-\-assets
List binary release assets for the given tag.
.TP
.B \-\-detect
Auto-detect the best binary asset for your OS and architecture,
highlighting the recommended download in the asset list.
.TP
.BI \-\-get " pattern"
Download the asset whose name matches
.IR pattern .
If multiple assets match, an interactive selection prompt is shown.
.TP
.B \-\-install
Download, extract, and install the binary to your PATH automatically
(\fI/usr/local/bin\fR when writable, else \fI~/.local/bin\fR or \fI~/bin\fR,
or the
.B \-\-dir
folder). The download and its extraction happen in a temporary folder.
Uses
.B \-\-detect
to find the right asset when no
.B \-\-get
pattern is given.
.TP
.BR \-\-releases ", " \-\-list
List all available releases for the repository. With
.BR \-\-json ,
prints the first ten releases as described in
.BR "JSON OUTPUT" .
.TP
.B \-\-source " zip|tar"
Download the source archive non-interactively.
Accepts
.B zip
or
.B tar
(tar.gz) as argument. Suitable for use in scripts.
.TP
.BR \-\-checksum ", " \-\-verify
Verify the SHA-256 checksum of the downloaded file after
.B \-\-get
or
.BR \-\-install .
Looks for a companion checksum file among the release assets.
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " folder"
Write the files of
.B \-\-get
and
.BR \-\-source ,
the interactive (z)ip/(t)ar download, and the binary of
.BR \-\-install ,
to
.I folder
instead of the working directory (or the PATH folder for
.BR \-\-install ).
The folder must already exist and be writable.
.TP
.B \-\-notes
Show the release notes for the resolved tag.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output release information as JSON, with the same keys whether the data comes
from the GitHub API (through
.BR gh )
or from the web pages. See
.BR "JSON OUTPUT" .
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Output the version tag only. Useful for scripting:
.B VERSION=$(gft nodejs/node -q)
.TP
.B \-\-pre
.PD 0
.TP
.B \-\-prerelease
.PD
Include pre-releases when resolving the latest tag.
By default, gft resolves to the latest stable release.
.TP
.B \-\-open
Open the release page in the default browser.
Combinable with other options (does not exit early).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colored output. Also honoured via the
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Bypass the local response cache for this invocation.
.TP
.B \-\-clear\-cache
Clear all cached responses and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
Commands are only recognised as the first argument: a repository or tag named
.BR update ,
.BR delete ,
.B uninstall
or
.B stash
is never taken for a command.
.TP
.B gft update
Upgrade gft to the latest version in-place. Alias:
.BR \-\-upgrade .
Under a package, prints the apt command to run and exits with status 1
without changing anything.
.TP
.B gft delete
Uninstall gft and remove all associated files. Alias:
.BR uninstall .
Under a package, prints
.B sudo apt remove gft
and exits with status 1 without changing anything.
.TP
.BI "gft stash " "[action]"
Manage git stashes in the repository at the current directory.
Available actions:
.RS
.TP
.B list
List all stashes (default when no action is given).
.TP
.BI "show " "[n]"
Show the diff of stash
.I n
(default: 0).
.TP
.BI "drop " "n"
Drop stash
.IR n .
Asks for confirmation unless
.B \-y
is passed.
.TP
.B clean
Delete all stashes. Alias:
.BR clear .
Asks for confirmation unless
.B \-y
is passed.
.RE
.RS
.PP
Option
.B \-y
/
.B \-\-yes
skips confirmation prompts (useful in scripts).
.RE
.SH PACKAGE INSTALLATION
The
.B gft
package for Debian and Ubuntu (one file for every architecture) installs
.IR /usr/bin/gft ,
the alias
.IR /usr/bin/gfv ,
the bash and zsh completions and this manual page. It is distributed as a
.I .deb
attached to each GitHub release, which is installed with
.BR "sudo apt install ./gft_<version>_all.deb" .
.PP
The package contains the marker
.IR /usr/share/gft/install-method ,
which gft reads at
.I ../share/gft/install-method
relative to the real location of the script. When it says
.BR install_method=apt ,
.BR "gft update" ,
.BR "gft \-\-upgrade" ,
.B gft delete
and
.B gft uninstall
change nothing: they print the apt command and exit with status 1. The command
depends on the
.B package=
line of the marker. For
.BR package=deb ,
the file attached to a GitHub release, the new
.I .deb
is downloaded from https://github.com/20syldev/gft/releases/latest and installed with
.BR "sudo apt install ./gft_<version>_all.deb" .
For
.B package=apt
and
.BR package=ppa ,
use
.BR "sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade gft" .
Removal is always
.BR "sudo apt remove gft" .
.PP
The
.B install.sh
installer and its companions
.B update.sh
and
.B delete.sh
refuse to run while the package is installed. Do not mix both ways of
installing gft.
.PP
Each GitHub release also carries
.I gft_<version>_checksums.txt
(the SHA-256 of the
.IR .deb )
and its minisign signature
.IR gft_<version>_checksums.txt.minisig ,
made with the key
.I packaging/minisign.pub
of the source repository at the release tag. To verify them:
.PP
.RS
.nf
curl \-fsSLO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/20syldev/gft/<version>/packaging/minisign.pub
minisign \-V \-H \-p minisign.pub \-m gft_<version>_checksums.txt
sha256sum \-\-strict \-c gft_<version>_checksums.txt
.fi
.RE
.SH JSON OUTPUT
.B gft
.I user/repo
.RI [ tag ]
.B \-\-json
prints one object (schema 1). The output is compact, on a single line with no
spaces, when standard output is not a terminal, and indented on a terminal.
Keys, always present and in this order:
.TP
.B schema
Integer, 1. Raised only on an incompatible change.
.TP
.BR repository ", " tag ", " name
Strings: the repository as given (under its current name when it was renamed
or transferred), the release tag, the release title (the tag when the release
has no title).
.TP
.B published_at
Publication date, ISO 8601 UTC (e.g. 2026\-11\-12T19:03:51Z), or null.
.TP
.B prerelease
Boolean.
.TP
.BR release_url ", " repo_url ", " zip_url ", " tarball_url
Strings.
.TP
.B source
.B \(dqapi\(dq
(read through
.BR gh )
or
.B \(dqweb\(dq
(read from the GitHub pages).
.TP
.B assets
Array of objects sorted by name, each with
.B name
and
.B url
(strings) and
.B digest
(\fB"sha256:..."\fR or null).
.PP
When the release cannot be found, nothing is printed on standard output, an
error goes to standard error and the exit status is 1.
.PP
.B gft
.I user/repo
.B \-\-releases \-\-json
prints an array (newest first, up to ten) of objects with
.BR tag ,
.BR name ,
.B published_at
and
.BR prerelease ,
typed as above; an empty array when the repository has no release.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to any value, disables colored output.
.TP
.B GITHUB_TOKEN
Read by
.BR gh (1),
when installed, to authenticate. gft itself does not use it.
.TP
.B GFT_CACHE_TTL
Cache time-to-live in seconds (default: 300). Responses are cached in
.I ~/.config/gft/cache/
to avoid redundant network requests.
.TP
.B GFT_NO_SPINNER
When set to any value, disables the loading spinner shown during network
operations. The spinner is written to standard error and is already
suppressed automatically when standard error is not a terminal.
.TP
.B GFT_ASCII
When set to any value, forces ASCII-only symbols instead of the Unicode
status and box-drawing glyphs. This fallback is applied automatically
when the locale does not advertise a UTF-8 character set.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/gft/
Configuration and data directory.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gft/VERSION
Installed version of gft.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gft/cache/
Cached HTTP responses (cleared by
.BR \-\-clear\-cache ).
.PP
Files of the package (see
.BR "PACKAGE INSTALLATION" ):
.TP
.I /usr/bin/gft
The script. \fI/usr/bin/gfv\fR is a symbolic link to it.
.TP
.I /usr/share/gft/install-method
Marker with exactly two lines, \fBinstall_method=apt\fR and
\fBpackage=\fR\fIkind\fR, where \fIkind\fR is \fBdeb\fR (file of the GitHub
release), \fBapt\fR (signed apt repository) or \fBppa\fR (Launchpad build).
Its presence makes gft leave upgrades and removal to apt.
.TP
.I /usr/share/bash-completion/completions/gft
Bash completion (also linked as \fIgfv\fR).
.TP
.I /usr/share/zsh/vendor-completions/_gft
Zsh completion.
.TP
.I /usr/share/man/man1/gft.1.gz
This manual page (also linked as \fIgfv.1.gz\fR).
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/gft/copyright
The MIT licence.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Get latest release info:
.B gft cli/cli
.TP
Get a specific version:
.B gft nodejs/node v22.0.0
.TP
List all binary assets:
.B gft cli/cli --assets
.TP
Auto-detect the right binary:
.B gft cli/cli --detect
.TP
Download a specific asset:
.B gft cli/cli --get linux-amd64.deb
.TP
Download and install automatically:
.B gft cli/cli --install
.TP
Get version string for scripting:
.B VERSION=$(gft nodejs/node -q)
.TP
List all releases:
.B gft cli/cli --releases
.TP
List releases including pre-releases:
.B gft cli/cli --pre --releases
.TP
Show release notes:
.B gft cli/cli --notes
.TP
JSON output:
.B gft cli/cli --json
.TP
Download source as tar.gz (non-interactive):
.B gft cli/cli --source tar
.TP
Download into a given folder:
.B gft cli/cli --get linux-amd64.tar.gz --dir ~/Downloads
.TP
Install the binary into a given folder:
.B gft junegunn/fzf --install --dir ~/.local/bin
.TP
Treat everything after \-\- as a repository or tag:
.B gft -- update/x
.TP
Download and verify checksum:
.B gft cli/cli --get linux-amd64.tar.gz --checksum
.TP
Compare two releases:
.B gft cli/cli v2.40.0..v2.50.0
.TP
Open release page in browser:
.B gft cli/cli --open
.TP
List git stashes in the current repo:
.B gft stash list
.TP
Show the diff of stash 1:
.B gft stash show 1
.TP
Drop stash 0 without confirmation:
.B gft stash drop 0 -y
.TP
Delete all stashes:
.B gft stash clean
.SH BUGS
Only public repositories are supported: gft checks the repository anonymously
on github.com, so a private repository is rejected even when
.B gh
is logged in.
.PP
Without
.BR \-\-pre ,
a tag containing a slash is cut at the slash when the latest release is
resolved; give the tag explicitly. With
.BR \-\-pre ,
.B \-q
prints the tag percent-encoded as in the GitHub page (\fBcore%40...\fR), while
.B \-\-json
decodes it.
.PP
.B \-\-releases
only covers the first page of releases (about ten).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1),
.BR gh (1)
